Let's think step by step and output the final answer within \boxed{}." With the BASE model obtain per-token log p_base under REF, NEG, POS and WIKI and the REF full-distribution entropy; then free it, load the NSD checkpoint and obtain per-token log p_nsd under REF only. Define Delta_t = log p_nsd(y_t) - log p_base(y_t) (both under REF), p_ref,t = p_base(y_t) under REF, gates G_c,t = max(0, p_c,t - p_ref,t) for c in {NEG, POS, WIKI}.

Step 4 (token classes, paper Appendix E): whitespace-only -> style; contains a digit, an operator among + - = * / < > × ÷ ≤ ≥ ≠, a LaTeX command \[A-Za-z]+, a double backslash, or one of $ ^ _ -> task; normalized form in {mod, prime, factor, gcd, lcm, log, ln, sin, cos, tan, exp, integral, sqrt, boxed, frac, sum, prod, pi, alpha, beta, gamma, theta, delta, lambda, mu, sigma, infty, leq, geq, neq, cdot, times, div} -> task; pure punctuation or newline -> style; normalized form in {therefore, so, thus, hence, then, because, since, wait, maybe, perhaps, seems, okay, ok, well, now, first, next, finally, actually, alternatively, however, step, answer, let, lets, is, are, us, we, the, a, an, of, to, for, in, on, by, at, as, and, or, but, if, yes, no, this, that, these, those, it, its, be, been, being, have, has, had, do, does, did, will, would, should, could, can, may} -> style; otherwise neutral (normalized form = lower-cased token string with leading spaces/punctuation stripped). Also flag reflection tokens (wait, actually, hmm, reconsider, rethink, re-examine, check, verify, double-check, revisit), connectives (therefore, so, thus, hence), digits, and tokens inside the final \boxed{}.

Step 5 (analysis). Exclude EOS tokens. Primary cells: p_ref bins [0,0.2), [0.2,0.4), [0.4,0.6), [0.6,0.8), [0.8,0.95) crossed with class {task, style, neutral}. Within each cell, gated tokens are those with G_NEG >= 0.02 and ungated tokens those with G_NEG = 0 (tokens with 0 < G_NEG < 0.02, the near-zero flicker the paper describes in Section 5.3, are excluded from the primary and reported separately); keep cells with at least 100 gated and 100 ungated tokens; d_cell = mean Delta(gated) - mean Delta(ungated). Primary statistic D_NEG = sum over kept cells of n_gated,cell * d_cell divided by sum of n_gated,cell. Compute D_POS and D_WIKI identically with their own gates, and D_NEG - D_POS, D_NEG - D_WIKI. Confidence intervals: 1000-resample cluster bootstrap over rollouts recomputing the full statistic. Secondary: the same with p_ref bins only (no class split) and with the [0.95, 1] bin; within-cell Spearman correlation between G_NEG and Delta among gated tokens; the Delta-versus-p_ref profile (mean Delta and mean |Delta| per p_ref bin of width 0.05; does suppression peak at mid confidence as the paper's Appendix A predicts?); mean Delta and mean |Delta| by class (style-task ratio of mean |Delta| across p_ref bins); mean Delta on reflection tokens, connectives, digits and boxed-answer tokens; the share of total negative Delta mass on NEG-gated tokens versus their share of tokens; fraction of tokens with Delta > 0; overall mean Delta and the mean change in entropy (NSD minus base, both under REF) by class; base rollout accuracy.

