Compute all pairwise churns per task and E. Uncertainty: 2000 bootstrap resamples of test items within tasks, applied jointly to all systems. Also report the min-max range of E over the alternative choices of same-spec pair, as a build-level spread that the item bootstrap misses.

Equivalence reading: if the CI of E lies within [-0.01, 0.01], rewording is reported as no worse than re-synthesis.

Meaning-preservation gate: compute teacher paraphrase churn, mean of churn(T_s0,T_s1) and churn(T_s0,T_s2), and teacher resampling churn, churn between the two temperature-1 samples. If paraphrase churn exceeds resampling churn by more than 0.05, the paraphrases are flagged as possibly meaning-shifting and E is reported with that caveat.

Secondary results:
- floor churn(A0,A0r);
- seed churn, the mean over pairs of {A0,A1,A2};
- re-synthesis churn minus seed churn, and per-task log ratios;
- data-only rewording effect, mean churn(P1x vs {A0,B0,C0}) minus same-spec churn;
- prompt-only effect, churn(P1,P1x);
- accuracy per build, with SD over {A0,B0,C0} and over {A0,A1,A2};
- accuracy of a majority vote over A0, B0 and C0;
- AUROC of teacher ambiguity for predicting items that differ between A0 and B0.

